/-!
## §I - Boundary-audited integration through Definitions 12--18

The paper uses the symbol `A_q` for objects living over two different bases:
Definition 12 is built over the radius interval, while Definition 15 is built
over the quotient `X`.  There is no paper-supplied continuous map identifying
those bases.  The bridge below therefore makes the weakest honest canonical
construction: global Definition-12 tensor sections form a constant presheaf
on `X`, and its canonical zero morphism lands in the actual modular-covariant
q-gauge sheaf.  No unproved equivalence of the two bases is asserted.

Both degenerate arrows are named `_zeroModel`.  Separate structures expose the
nontrivial cross-base map and the q-gauge-to-DGA realization that would be
needed for the literal paper bridge.  Independently of those missing data,
the actual Definition-14 equalizer, Proposition-20 global sections, the
standalone Proposition-15 functor, and the Proposition-21 derived Tor object
are connected at their precisely typed common interfaces.
-/

namespace PaperElementaryIntegration

noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory
open MeasureTheory
open Definition18Proposition19ActualSpecialization

abbrev Base := Proposition20ActualQGaugeSpecialization.Base
abbrev Opens := Proposition20ActualQGaugeSpecialization.Opens
